# Archives & backups
*.zip
# …except the archives the Rust zip reader is tested against. They are INPUTS, written
# by another tool (Python's zipfile) so the decompressor is not merely reading its own
# output, and one of them is a deliberate path-traversal archive the extractor must
# refuse. Frozen bytes, not build output — the blanket rule above swallowed them, and
# CI spent its whole life red because a fresh checkout had no fixtures to read.
!rust/tests/data/*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bak
*.orig

