# Internal working docs: plans, specs, decisions and the pre-site user docs.
# Kept out of the repository on purpose; versioned by its own git inside.
temp_docs/

# Rust
rust/target/

# The starter data packs, copied in by `rust/scripts/bundle-packs.mjs` only long
# enough to build the crate. The packs live once, at data/packs; a second copy
# committed here would shadow the real one and go quietly out of date. Cargo is
# told to package them anyway through `include` in rust/Cargo.toml, which does
# not consult this file.
rust/src/packs/bundled/

# The same, for C#: `csharp/scripts/bundle-packs.mjs` stages the starter packs
# here only long enough for `dotnet pack` to embed them in the assembly.
csharp/Tdcv2/PacksData/

# --- Local-only: AI assistant state, scratch files ---------------------------
# These are created by the tools a developer happens to use and say nothing about
# the project. They must never reach the tree.
.claude/
.superpowers/
.codex/
.cursor/
.aider*
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Scratch configs for trying things out. Nothing here is part of the product;
# `./run <file>` takes any path, so nothing in the repo depends on them.
playground/
playground.tdc
probe.tdc
scratch/
*.scratch.tdc

# Docusaurus build output and cache. `docs/` is the committed export; the built
# site is regenerated by `npm --prefix webdoc run build`.
webdoc/build/
webdoc/.docusaurus/
webdoc/review-bundle/
webdoc/*.zip
